course: dictionary
lesson: 12477
title: Deity
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A deity is a god or goddess. You will meet this word in history, religion and myth lessons, where people tell stories about the gods they believed in. «The ancient Greeks believed Zeus was the king of the deities.» The words around deities give you the clue: Greeks, king and myths all point to gods.
explain: Deities is the plural, which means more than one. One deity, two or more deities. Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: «The ancient Greeks believed Zeus was the king of the gods» still makes sense, so deity means god or goddess.
explain: Myths often name a deity and tell what they did. «In the myth, the goddess Athena helped the hero.» Athena is a goddess, so she is a deity. Stories from different places have different deities, such as Egyptian, Roman and Hindu ones.
fact: A deity is a god or goddess.
fact: «Deities» is the plural of «deity»: one deity, many deities.
fact: Deities appear in myths, religion lessons and history lessons about Greece, Rome, Egypt and India.
fact: «Zeus» and «Athena» are Greek deities; «Ra» is an Egyptian deity who was the sun god.
fact: Context clues such as «myth», «Greeks» or «god» help you work out what a deity is.
exercise: «The ancient Greeks believed Zeus was the king of the deities.» What does deities mean? | Kings and queens | *Gods and goddesses | Animals in a forest | Heroes and soldiers
exercise: Find and copy the word for a god or goddess in: «Egyptians prayed to many deities, such as Ra.» | many | *deities | Egyptians | prayed
exercise: Lily says, «A deity is just a statue in a museum.» Is she right? | No, a deity is a type of food | *No, a deity is a god or goddess | Yes, a deity is a museum | Yes, a deity is a statue
test: «In the myth, the goddess Athena helped the hero.» What kind of being is Athena in this myth? | *A deity | A king from a castle | A monster from the sea | A mortal woman who lives in a village
test: What is the plural of deity? | deitee | *deities | deitys | deity's
exam: Which word means the same as deity? | *God | Temple | Myth | Hero
